Hey all

I've come back to nethack recently after taking an extended break for
a couple of years. I've been playing again for about 3 weeks, and it's
taken me a while to get back into the swing of it. I've ascended a
couple of times before, and posted one of those up on this newsgroup.
I'd include the url to the archive, but It's long and I don't want to
offend by wrapping the past badly :)

I just comleted my first (semi)successful protection run. Figured it
might make a good story to anyone feeling bored ;-)...

I only started this game 'cause I wasn't very sober and didn't want to
mess up my current main game with a rogue nearing the bottom of the
mines... that's been a tough game so far, but I've been managing quite
well to date. So I started the game with the name "Vetch" instead of
my own name, "Sam", as I usually do. I chose a Lawful Male Monk.

Vetch started with a magic makrer and a scroll of id... it's been so
long since I played a monk that I can't remember if this is normal
for a monk, so I'm mentioning it here for interest's sake. First thing
I found was a pair of buckled boots that weren't cursed and turned out
to be speed boots!   Damn it, that's the second time in two weeks I
started a game not expecting to play seiously and then been given speed
boots a short while later! The RNG knows what I'm thinking, I know it
does.

Well, there was no playing frivolously now, as I was intending to do,
so I decided to try the minetown protection run.  I'd only killed a
newt on the first level, so I let my cat, Farrow do all the killing
from there... and boy, it takes a lot of patience! I don't know how the
pacifists can stomach it ;-)...

I found a leash, whistle and key on the first couple of levels. They
all came in handy for pet control and threat reduction. On level 2,
I encountered a gas spore in a tight spot, and Farrow didn't want to
touch it. There was no way around it, so not wanting to risk taking
the full blast from it, I ran along a long corridor into a larger room
and managed to get around it, once it was in the room. I ran back out,
and locked the door. If I survived the minetown run I could sort it out
later.

With a great deal of careful playing and patience, Farrow and I found
the mine entrance halfway through our exploration of DL4. I wanted to
finish exploring DL4 to find more gold (I had 280gp by that time) but
as i was allowing Farrow to lead me along a corridor, he attacked
something in front of him and suddenly became very hot. I didn't want
to risk losing Farrow to a red mold, and there was no way further
forward, so I was forced to enter the mines.

The first level was dark, and I had no light source. I took a few steps
and started to explore. Farrow killed a gnome, and while he was eating
his corpse I had to rely on Elbereth to scare off a few gnomes. The
next
thing I knew, Farrow was dead! But there was no time to mourn, the
gnomes
were closing in. I was still only a few steps from the stairs out. I
could have aborted mission...

But I decided to give it a try anyway. I was very fast, and the speed
boots and an orcish helm I found had lowered my AC to 2, which wasn't
too bad for a starting monk (though I'm likely to be told otherwise,
probably ;-) ). I wanted to see if some very careful playing could
see me through to minetown.

I started following the edge of the wall I'd descended close to. A few
more nomes came up, but I found that being so fast allowed me to write
'elbereth' in the dust several times before they could move, so I had
several goes at getting it right in time. That helped a lot. I found
myself being backed intoa corner that I strongly suspected did NOT
contain the stairs down, but as I stepepd away from a gnome lord,
backing up to the wall, the floor gave way beneath me and I fell
through a trapdoor!

Found myself in a small space on another dark level, the next level
down. The single exit led along a long corridor, over an arrow trap
(I honestly didn't feel like I had the time to search for traps - I
didn't want to get hemmed in) and out into a larger space. I found
myself at the receiving end of thrown daggers from both directions,
in a wide corridor area. I Picked up the daggers to make sure they
weren't thrown at me again, picked the direction I felt most lucky
travelling in and ran in that diraection, pausing a few times to
hurredly scribble the name of Elbereth again, when I foundmyself
face to face with the gnomes in that direction. I was hit by a salvo
of daggers again from behind, and had to drink one of my potions of
healing.

It turned out I was lucky (again) and with a crowd of diminuitive and
rather ugly enraged gnomes at my heels, I came upon the stairs down,
and beleiving this might be the entrance to mine town, I gleefully
escaped the mob.

I was in the dark again, with a sinking feeling that there was another
level of this. Taking a couple of steps toward the closest edge of
the level, I found myself next to a long staright wall. Perhaps I
was actually in minetown, and this was just a dark room? I took a
step north.

Nope. This is the mines still. Another dark level, evading these
brutes awaited. My search conitinued for the hallowed ">" that would
take me one step closer to the preist that awaited below.

Things got very sticky on this level. I lost times of the number of
times I invoked the name of that fair Elven lady, as I found myself
being chased back and forth this time across the level. One of them
had a crossbow, and I was forced to use my other two potions of
healing before he ran out of bolts to fire at me. I stood on a
landmine at one point, but had full health at the time. It took me
for 15 hp to 6 hp and left me at the bottom of a pit, as the closed
in. I was getting better at judging how long I had to dodge around
the gnomes by now, though. I didn't have to write the name every
time i found myself in frong of them. I was much faster than the
were. The level was split into two major sections by a long narror
corridor at the middle. I came down on the right, and searched that
entire section before realising I would have to dodge around the
crowd again to get to the other part of the level. I managed, and
my health was slowlya and surely bulding up again. Having and idea
as I ran alon the narrow passage, I dropped a sling and wrote the
'E' word several times in quick succession on the ground beside it.
That should hold them off for a while.

My search of this section was quieter at first - most of the gnomes
had gone to the other side of the level.  I didn't let myself get
complacent, though, and that was a very good thing, as a momanet
later, three giant ants scuttled into my light range.

Now, I knew that these guys are fast too, I can't dodge them as
easily as gnomes. I guess the RNG had decided to up-the-ante a
little here. I was lucky scribbling in the dust the first time, and
that bought me a quick breather running along a wall at the left
side of the level, one of them found me again, and bit me. It took
me to 2hp, and I had no potions left. I prayed...

Shan Lai Ching was well-pleased, and returned me to full hitpoints.
Phew! It seemd I still had another tick act bafore the ant could.
Engraved again, and the ant ran for it, rather than face a monk
stood over that name. I took another step, and as I did, I was
next to the other two ants. and there, in sight, were the stairs!
I moved onto them and away from the ants. They moved with me,
snapping at my heels. But it was too late. I was already escaping
down the stars...

To find myself in a lit, large square room. Woohoo! I was on the
level, now I just had to get to the priest! The corridors were
empty. I saw  a couple of gnomish wizards in one of the side rooms
through an open foor once i reached the town, but quickly closed
and locked the door before they could reach me. I dodged a gnomish
lord with a bow, taking an arrow, and into the general store. Somewhere
I had picked up another pair of boots, and an orange spellbook.
Deciding that I could buy it back later if I needed it, I sold
it and the boots for 156 gp (was only offered 6 gold for them)

+I ran to the temple, dodging the gnome lord again, taking another
arrow, and into the temple, locking the door. I gave the priest all
of my money, a paltry 450 odd gp and was rewarded just 2 points of
protection. I guess if my pet had survived I would have had more
money to give to the priest, but I hadn't been so lucky. At least
I'd managed it. I couls now proudly say I'd suceeded in completing
a protection run.

I'm now in minetown with no money, 0 AC and am level 6 after killing
2 gnome lords, an iguana, 2 gnomish wizards and a rothe. It's gonna
be interesting to see if I can manage to survive the trip back up
to the chest I've stashed my scroll of identify and a few other
cheap but useful items in back on level 2...

